"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Fricassee or fricassée  is a stew made with pieces of meat that have been browned in butter, then served in a sauce flavored with the cooking stock. Fricassee is usually made with chicken, veal or rabbit, with variations limited only by the ingredients the cook has at hand."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fricassee"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fricassee"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["White meat","ingredient/white-meat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Bayonne ham","dish/bayonne-ham"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Blanquette de veau","dish/blanquette-de-veau"],["Blini","dish/blini"],