ak cuisine in Indonesia that is usually served at certain customary feasts."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-manuk-napinadar"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuk_napinadar"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":11,"links":[["Andaliman","ingredient/andaliman"],["Ayam Kampong","ingredient/ayam-kampong"],["Bird's eye chili","ingredient/bird-s-eye-chili"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}]},"ingredient/brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia","n":"Brassica oleracea var. palmifolia","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Lacinato kale, also known as Tuscan kale, Italian kale, dinosaur kale,  kale, flat back kale, palm tree kale, black Tuscan palm, or, in Italian and often in English, cavolo nero, is a variety of kale from the Acephala group of cultivars Brassica oleracea grown for its edible leaves. Lacinato has a long tradition in Italian cuisine, especially that of Tuscany, where it has been grown for centuries, and it is one of the traditional ingredients of minestrone and ribollita."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacinato_kale"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Tuscan cuisine","cuisine/tuscan-cuisine",[["Ribollita","dish/ribollita"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Kidney bean","ingredient/kidney-bean"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/d/dd/Brassica_-_Gardenology.org-IMG_0606_bbg09.jpg/500px-Brassica_-_Gardenology.org-IMG_0606_bbg09.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Raffi Kojian","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brassica_-_Gardenology.org-IMG_0606_bbg09.jpg"}},"ingredient/bialy-bread":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bialy-bread","n":"Bialy (bread)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Bialy  is a type of bread roll, in which the center is indented and is traditionally covered with chopped onion and sprinkled with poppy seeds. The bialy was a part of the traditional Ashkenazi cuisine of the Jewish population of the city of Białystok in Poland until the destruction of the community during the Holocaust. Jewish immigrants brought the bialy to New York City, where it remains popular as an alternative to the bagel. It has become available, to a lesser extent, in other cities in the United States and elsewhere, and with additional or different flavorings and toppings."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bialy-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bialy_(bread)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Pacific Northwest cuisine","cuisine/pacific-northwest-cuisine",[["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]],["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states",[["Seattle-style hot dog","dish/seattle-style-hot-dog"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bialy","ingredient/bialy"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Hot dog bun","ingredient/hot-dog-bun"],["Sautéed onions","ingredient/sauteed-onions"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/0/03/KOSSAR_BIALY-18.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"EGiniger1","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KOSSAR_BIALY-18.jpg"}},"dish/sweet-and-sour-pork":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sweet-and-sour-pork","n":"Sweet and sour pork","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cantonese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sweet and sour pork is a Cantonese and Chinese-American dish consisting of fried pork tenders with sweet and sour sauce. It is usually served with vegetables, and sometimes with pineapple. The dish originated from Cantonese cuisine in the 18th century. It became popular in the United States after Chinese immigrants came to the US to work on railroads in the early 20th century."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sweet-and-sour-pork"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_and_sour_pork"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cantonese cuisine","cuisine/cantonese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Pineapple","ingredient/pineapple"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Sweet and sour","ingredient/sweet-and-sour"],["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Made With Lau","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"madewithlau.com","note":"Family-run channel and site teaching Cantonese recipes from retired chef Daddy Lau.","url":"https://madewithlau.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Cantonese cuisine","links":[["Cantonese restaurant","dish/cantonese-restaurant"],["Char siu","dish/char-siu"],["Har gow","dish/har-gow"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Lap cheong","dish/lap-cheong"],["Rice noodle roll","dish/rice-noodle-roll"],["Siu mei","dish/siu-mei"],["Turnip cake","dish/turnip-cake"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b7/%E8%8F%A0%E8%90%9D%E5%92%95%E5%99%9C%E8%82%89.jpg/500px-%E8%8F%A0%E8%90%9D%E5%92%95%E5%99%9C%E8%82%89.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Walter Grassroot","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%8F%A0%E8%90%9D%E5%92%95%E5%99%9C%E8%82%89.jpg"}},"dish/tsukemono":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tsukemono","n":"Tsukemono","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tsukemono, oshinko or konomono are Japanese preserved vegetables (usually pickled in salt, brine, or a bed of rice bran). They are served with rice as an okazu (side dish), with drinks as an otsumami (snack), as an accompaniment to or garnish for meals, and as a course in the kaiseki portion of a Japanese tea ceremony."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tsukemono"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukemono"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-noodles"],["Japanese restaurant","dish/japanese-restaurant"],["Japanese tea","dish/japanese-tea"],["Jingisukan","dish/jingisukan"],["Kaki furai","dish/kaki-furai"],["Kamaboko","dish/kamaboko"],["Kōji (food)","dish/koji-food"],["Kusa mochi","dish/kusa-mochi"],["Kushikatsu","dish/kushikatsu"],["List of Japanese restaurants","dish/list-of-japanese-restaurants"],["Makizushi","dish/makizushi"],["Miso","dish/miso"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Monjayaki","dish/monjayaki"],["Nikujaga","dish/nikujaga"],["Nimono","dish/nimono"],["Oden","dish/oden"],["Onigiri","dish/onigiri"],["Osechi","dish/osechi"],["Oyakodon","dish/oyakodon"],["Rainbow roll","dish/rainbow-roll"],["Ramen","dish/ramen"],["Ryōtei","dish/ryotei"],["Sashimi","dish/sashimi"],["Sencha","dish/sencha"],["Shizuoka oden","dish/shizuoka-oden"],["Sumiso","dish/sumiso"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/8/84/Tsukemono.jpg/500px-Tsukemono.jpg","w":500,"h":433,"by":"Mini923 at English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsukemono.jpg"}}}